body:
CSV export currently escapes commas/quotes/newlines but does not sanitize values for spreadsheet formula injection (e.g., cells starting with '=', '+', '-', '@', '|'). This can be exploited when opening exports in Excel/Sheets. Consider adding the same sanitization used in `packages/plugin-report/src/ReportExportEngine.ts` (prefix potentially dangerous leading characters) before escaping/quoting.
```suggestion
      const sanitized = str && /^[=+\-@|]/.test(str) ? `'${str}` : str;
      return sanitized.includes(',') || sanitized.includes('"') || sanitized.includes('\n') || sanitized.includes('\r')
        ? `"${sanitized.replace(/"/g, '""')}"`
        : sanitized;
```
